  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Long-term acoustic monitoring of critical forest elephant populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grantee is developing and expanding the use of acoustic recording devices in providing information about imperiled forest elephants that are very difficult or costly to monitor by direct observation or traditional transects. This grant will train Gabonese and Congolese students in monitoring and analyzing elephant activity at five sites (Jobo/Djoumou River, Precious Woods, Langoue Bai, Kessala, and northern Congo bais), and will further develop a tool to analyze elephant calls on recordings to interpret data more easily and rapidly for long-term elephant population monitoring.</narrative>
  </description>
